WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
- [Kelly] So, your family was so cute

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.080
when they watched you win gold in Tokyo.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:04.913
I can only imagine.

00:00:04.913 --> 00:00:07.870
So, who had the best
reaction when you got home?

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:09.750
- I think definitely my sister.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.240
She's been like my best friend.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.240
Of course I was super
excited to see my dad

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.073
and my mom,

00:00:14.073 --> 00:00:16.520
because they have basically supported me

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:17.710
throughout the whole thing.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:18.543
- And I was so excited to wrap the medals

00:00:18.543 --> 00:00:20.200
around their neck,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.510
but I think just being with my sister

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.000
was like the most amazing thing,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.970
because she's my best friend.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.069
- [Kelly] Oh, that's amazing!

00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:27.902
(audience clapping)

00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:29.840
How far apart are you on age?

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.110
- We are actually a week and a half apart.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:33.943
She's my step-sister,

00:00:33.943 --> 00:00:35.001
but we're...
- I was like...

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:35.834
I wish you could have
been in my head just then.

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:39.309
I was like, "Wait, what?"

00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:40.480
(guest giggles)

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.019
I was like (indistinct)

00:00:42.019 --> 00:00:42.852
Oh, that's amazing!

00:00:42.852 --> 00:00:43.685
- Yeah! So, we're really close.

00:00:43.685 --> 00:00:44.518
- Hey! Blended families
are hard sometimes,

00:00:44.518 --> 00:00:45.990
so, that's amazing
you're all are so close.

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.110
That's cool.
- We used to hate each other

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:49.099
when we were younger.
- [Kelly] See? That happens.

00:00:49.099 --> 00:00:50.120
(audience laughing)

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:50.953
You know what?

00:00:50.953 --> 00:00:51.786
Thank you though, I have young kids,

00:00:51.786 --> 00:00:52.848
they hate each other sometimes,

00:00:52.848 --> 00:00:53.681
and I'm like, "You're
going to like each other,

00:00:53.681 --> 00:00:54.514
"one day, right?"
- Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:54.514 --> 00:00:55.347
- [Kelly] Okay, cool.

00:00:55.347 --> 00:00:56.180
(guest giggling)

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.250
Yeah! So, do you have any rituals

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.810
before you compete?

00:00:58.810 --> 00:00:59.830
- I have to get ready,

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:02.690
like two hours earlier.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.160
I have to listen to the same song.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.353
- [Kelly] Oh my God!

00:01:05.353 --> 00:01:06.186
You're like my sister in an airport.

00:01:06.186 --> 00:01:07.019
(guest giggles)

00:01:07.019 --> 00:01:08.410
She used to be there like forever before.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.150
- I know and I'm usually always late so...

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:10.983
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:10.983 --> 00:01:11.830
Well, what song do you listen to

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:12.663
before you compete?

00:01:12.663 --> 00:01:14.460
I get like amped up before my shows

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.000
- Same, it's always like rap
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.620
Oh my God! That is so funny,

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:20.580
I love the most opposite of me.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.227
I'm like, "Yes Jay-Z!

00:01:22.227 --> 00:01:23.720
"I'm ready!"

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:24.710
I'm amped up.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.250
There's something about the beat.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.078
Like all their beats.
- It just makes you like,

00:01:28.078 --> 00:01:28.911
so hyped before you go.

00:01:28.911 --> 00:01:29.900
This is exactly what I need
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.170
Yes, absolutely.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.810
Do you do any ritual before you act,

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.300
or anything?

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.340
- Well, music is always a way in for me.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:39.010
I always make a playlist
for my characters.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.040
- [Kelly] Oh, I love that!
- Yup! Yup! Yup!

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.020
- [Kelly] That's smart.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.180
Because it does get you in the mood.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.480
- Totally.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.313
Totally.

00:01:44.313 --> 00:01:45.146
- That's clever.
- Yup!

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:46.119
- [Kelly] Everyone's
stealing that idea right now.

00:01:46.119 --> 00:01:46.952
(audience laughs)

00:01:46.952 --> 00:01:47.785
- Okay.

00:01:47.785 --> 00:01:48.618
So you're on "Dancing with the Stars" now,

00:01:48.618 --> 00:01:50.540
and there's a history of elite athletes

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:51.819
like winning.

00:01:51.819 --> 00:01:53.990
Do you think it's unfair

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:55.200
'cause you're so athletic,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.050
like going against people

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:59.019
that are maybe similar
to how in shape I am?

00:01:59.019 --> 00:02:01.779
- Okay, really?

00:02:01.779 --> 00:02:02.939
(everybody laughing)

00:02:02.939 --> 00:02:03.772
- But dancing is different.

00:02:03.772 --> 00:02:04.760
- Yeah! And the whole cast though,

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.429
I feel like is dancers.

00:02:06.429 --> 00:02:08.370
So, everybody kind of has experience,

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:09.203
but...
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:09.203 --> 00:02:10.680
- The most dancing I do is on the floor,

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.490
when I'm trying to distract
everybody and myself

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:14.068
from thinking about landing on my face.

00:02:14.068 --> 00:02:15.080
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:15.913
So, I don't know.

00:02:15.913 --> 00:02:16.746
Like it's just very different.

00:02:16.746 --> 00:02:17.579
I never had dance class,

00:02:17.579 --> 00:02:19.380
but it's been really fun lately.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.510
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:21.820
You feel confident as a dancer?

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:22.780
Like, when you're out there?

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.010
I sometimes on stage

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.630
become like this super confident person.

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:27.880
Like, I'm a confident person in life,

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:28.830
but I feel like when you're on stage,

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:29.700
and you're like doing stuff,

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.128
you feel like, "I'm Jay-Z".
- [Guest] No.

00:02:32.128 --> 00:02:33.669
I'm so nervous.

00:02:33.669 --> 00:02:34.502
(everyone laughs)

00:02:34.502 --> 00:02:35.459
- [Kelly] Oh you do?
- Yes.

00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:36.292
I mean when I'm competing for gymnastics,

00:02:36.292 --> 00:02:38.033
I'm completely fine,

00:02:39.268 --> 00:02:40.340
but this is like something
I'd never done before.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:41.210
So, when I'm doing it,

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:42.043
I'm like, "Oh my God!"

00:02:42.043 --> 00:02:45.179
I'm shaking and stuff in the back.

00:02:45.179 --> 00:02:46.300
But I feel like I also just stress,

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.133
because I like,

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.270
don't practice enough,

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.910
because gymnastics I'm used to practicing

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:51.930
like seven hours.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:54.460
- This is like three hours.

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:56.059
- That sounds like workout though.

00:02:56.059 --> 00:02:56.892
(guests laughing)

00:02:56.892 --> 00:02:58.270
That sounds hard.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:02:59.103
I love that you get nervous,

00:02:59.103 --> 00:03:00.320
so, that's good that
you're telling us that,

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.440
because we just think of you as like,

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.860
superheroes and you do anything

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.200
and you're fine all the time.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.300
So, you get nervous with it?

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.460
That makes me feel good.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:07.462
- [Guest] Yeah.

00:03:07.462 --> 00:03:08.295
(everyone laughs)

00:03:08.295 --> 00:03:09.128
- I feel better now.

00:03:09.128 --> 00:03:10.360
I'm sorry for you.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:11.590
- Usually, I have to
puke every time before

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:12.423
- [Kelly] Oh my God!

00:03:12.423 --> 00:03:16.103
That's so horrible.
(everyone laughing)

